On Fri, 29 Aug 2003, Frank Roberts - SOTL wrote:

> > >+ I have been principally using KDE.
> > >+ I have Gnome configures.
> > >+ So I decided to configure Ice-WM.
> > >+ Does anyone know how to configure the desktop by adding different
> > >backgrounds
> > >+ add icons to Ice-WM?
> > >
You need to look for the configuration files "preferences", "menu" and/or
"toolbar".  These will be located under either under ~/icewm or ~/.icewm
or in the global ?/icewm.  I'm sorry to report that I can't tell you at
the moment where the global dir is located.  The files mentioned need to
be ferretted through and edited to your liking (they're 
well-commented).  There are also gui front-ends for modifying the config
files, but I can't tell you the name of it/them at the moment,
unfortunately.  Sorry if this is not much help for you.  I've fiddled a
bit with configuring icewm, but don't consider myself any sort of expert
at it.  I never did figure out how to place shortcuts/symlinks on the
desktop.

James

